Q1. Open Power Query Editor (PQE) in Power BI and load a sample dataset of IPL cricket matches (download from Kaggle or use any CSV with match details).
Ans:- Steps:
Open Power BI Desktop.
Click Home → Get Data → Text/CSV.
Select the IPL matches CSV file.
In the preview window, click Transform Data.
Power Query Editor will open.
Check the columns and data in the dataset.

Q2. In PQE, remove all columns except for 'Team 1', 'Team 2', 'Winner', and 'Venue' to focus only on the most relevant details for a quick match summary.
Ans:- We need only four columns:
Team 1
Team 2
Winner
Venue
Steps:
Select Team 1.
Hold Ctrl and select Team 2, Winner, and Venue.
Right-click on any selected column.
Select Remove Other Columns.
Now only the four required columns will remain.

Q3. Use the Remove Rows feature in PQE to delete the first 2 rows and any rows where the 'Winner' column is null or empty.
Ans:- A. Remove First 2 Rows
Go to Home → Remove Rows.
Select Remove Top Rows.
Enter 2.
Click OK.

The first two rows will be deleted.

B. Remove Null/Empty Winner Rows
Click the filter arrow on the Winner column.
Find (null) or blank values.
Uncheck the null/blank value.
Click OK.
Now only rows with a valid Winner value will remain.

Q4. Find and remove duplicate rows in your IPL dataset based on 'Team 1', 'Team 2', and 'Venue' columns.<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Use the 'Remove Duplicates' option after selecting these columns.</em>
Ans:- We need to remove duplicate rows based on:

Team 1 + Team 2 + Venue

Steps:
Select the Team 1 column.
Hold Ctrl and select Team 2 and Venue.
Go to Home → Remove Rows → Remove Duplicates.

Power Query will keep the first occurrence and remove the duplicate combinations.

Q5. Handle any error rows in your dataset by replacing errors in the 'Winner' column with the value 'Unknown', then load the cleaned data to Power BI.
<br><br><em><strong>Hint:</strong> Right-click the column and use 'Replace Errors'.</em>
Ans:- If the Winner column contains error values, we need to replace those errors with Unknown.
Steps:
Right-click the Winner column.
Select Replace Errors.
Enter:

Unknown
Click OK.
The errors in the Winner column will now be replaced with Unknown.
